# Assignment review evidence — 2026-10-05

## Coordination routing — 2026-10-06

The [coordination-loop](../tickets/done/01-0004-coordination-loop.md) retains review's
original-issue evidence and acceptance duties, adds explicit routes for findings
and reuses an active review on coordinator re-entry. Local L14 has one review
home. [Coordination evidence](coordinate.evidence.md) records independently graded
blockers, timeline references, changed prerequisites, resumption and evidence limits.
This does not establish recipient-host invocation or publish the new instructions.

Declared while implementing
[workshop-coordination-ready](../tickets/01-0005-workshop-coordination-ready.md).
The user accepted original-issue communication, conversation-held review history,
inspectable recipient evidence, the after-recall entry sequence and returning to
agreed work after handling findings. The
[exchange contract](../agent-contract.md#exchange-through-github-issues) holds these
agreements. This record separates installed instructions from observed invocation
and independent judgment.

## Installed shape

The [review skill](../../.agents/skills/review-assignments/SKILL.md) discovers issued
assignments and incoming requests in all issue states, inspects conversation and
closure history, and handles the findings through installed local rule L14.
L14 is authored once and installed in both review and reconciliation. L15 invokes
review after recall through AGENTS.md. Context comes from the local source pointers.
The new declaration and maintenance binding use the existing harness mechanisms.
No separate acknowledgement ledger or polling service was introduced.

