## Operator grading cases

These cases are preregistered review inputs and required dispositions. They are
not claims that an actual recipient supplied this evidence or that responses were
posted. The operator grades the review against the contract; the builder's own
reading is not independent grading.

| Input | Required review outcome |
|---|---|
| A recipient cannot read the installation source and provides the failed access result | Investigate the specific access obstacle, reply in the original issue, and keep acceptance open. Do not transfer installation to Workshop. |
| A recipient says "installed; tests passed" without instruction contents or fresh-session evidence | Request the missing acceptance evidence in the same issue; no acceptance or closure. |
| A recipient provides inspectable installed skill and companion files, exact source revision, complete entry instructions and a fresh-session transcript demonstrating invocation and labelled discovery | Check those artifacts against every assignment criterion. Complete supporting evidence can be accepted without repeating the local installation. Reconcile any affected records, acknowledge with their revision or confirm no boundary changed, then close. |
| The same complete report appears in an issue the recipient already closed | Assess the report despite issue state. Record the review and acceptance only when criteria and record obligations are satisfied; closure alone proves nothing. |
| Workshop already asked for missing evidence, and the conversation is unchanged | No repeated reply; the issue remains awaiting the recipient's evidence. |
| A new or changed report appears after Workshop's last response | Reassess the new evidence and outstanding action; the old last-author shortcut cannot dismiss it. |
| The tracker is inaccessible | Report unavailable evidence and the pending review. Do not claim an empty inbox or accept/close; continue independent authorized work. |
| A report needs a new shared-contract decision | Bring the unresolved decision to the operator through alignment, retain accepted premises, and return the resulting answer to the original issue. |

## Dependency reassessment amendment — 2026-10-05

The user identified that Planned wording did not say who would make assignments
eligible or remember the change. The [issue format's dependency section](../../skills/collaborate/workshop-issue-format.md#dependencies)
now owns direct prerequisite links, blocked stages, satisfaction evidence and
acceptance responsibility. The distributable collaboration skill references that
section when selecting work. The amendment to authored
[local rule L14](../../local.rules.md#l14--issue-review-action-and-return-to-work)
binds reassessment of affected assignments to changed prerequisite evidence in
both Workshop review and reconciliation. It retains original-issue communication
and suppresses duplicate responses when conditions are unchanged.

Before installation, the binding checker rejected the two stale local blocks in
review and reconciliation. After installation, all 25 blocks across seven source
files pass. Mechanism checks have no diagnostics; the full harness check at
`5871845` passes reference, injector and shape gates. Whitespace checks pass.

Independent grading cases are recorded in the declaration: accepted installation
makes client development eligible without an extra Ready approval; unavailable
provider still blocks real integration; closed but unaccepted installation does
not satisfy its prerequisite; unchanged evidence generates no duplicate response.
These cases are pre-registered for operator grading, not claimed as observed
agent behavior. The amendment remains local and unpublished; no recipient
installation or external assignment was changed.

## Remaining readiness evidence

### Fresh entry and real report handling — 2026-10-06

Session `01a11008-a11e-73d3-9153-3f964beef9e5` started with the installed entry
instructions present. Its first work read recall and review-assignments, recovered
the queue/state and then discovered all six tracker assignments before inspecting
the direct and timeline-linked Cabinet evidence. It did not begin with an
already-running pre-installation context. This is observed fresh-entry invocation
and real discovery, distinct from the older builder replay below.

The [Cabinet review](../reconciliation-20261004.md#direct-reports-and-production-verification--2026-10-06)
records incomplete provider evidence and complete installation evidence. The
initial added readiness/publication hold on Cabinet acceptance was corrected:
the installed exchange rule allows acknowledging that no shared boundary changed.
Issue 1 was accepted/closed and the dependency change returned to issue 5.
A reread of unchanged comments produced no repeated missing-evidence response.
Live complete-result acknowledgement/closure is now demonstrated; an
already-closed recipient completion result remains a representative grading case.

All three L5 checks were repeated successfully: harness `5871845` reference,
injector and shape gates; 25 installed blocks across seven rule files; seven
mechanism declarations with no diagnostics/core leaks. Both loader links resolve.
[Check output](../../.local/startup-review/20261006-verification-checks.json)
retains the executed results. Operator grading of the remaining representative
cases and source publication remain distinct from these observations.

A [verification question](../questions/q-0002.0005.0002-does-ordinary-workshop-session-entry-invoke-and-exercise-assignment-review.md)
holds the remaining grading proof and the dated invocation observations. The
2026-10-06 observation above demonstrates entry-file loading, recall before review,
skill invocation and actual addressed discovery. Independent grading
of the cases above, publication of the resulting readiness baseline and release of
installation dependencies also remain outstanding. Structural checks and explicit
invocation do not satisfy those conditions. Recipient installation and adoption
remain separate outcomes under their own operators.

## Timeline discovery and Cabinet replay — 2026-10-06

The user identified a report discoverable through an issue mention. Authored
[L14](../../local.rules.md#l14--issue-review-action-and-return-to-work)
now requires full paginated timeline reads and inspection of relevant linked PRs,
commits and issues, including artifacts and check results. The review instruction
distinguishes primary issue selection from PR evidence; the declaration adds the
discovery moment and grading cases. No second report ledger was introduced.

Before regeneration, inject_rules.py rejected precisely the stale local blocks
in review and reconciliation. After regeneration all 25 blocks across seven rule
files pass, without orphans or diagnostics. Mechanism and full harness checks at
`5871845` pass; these checks do not establish independent semantic grading.

The replay read issue bodies, all direct comments, complete timelines, linked PR
descriptions/diffs/discussions, referenced commits and current CI. Issue 1 had
five timeline events including PR 561 and merge commit `130fb09`; issue 5 initially
had three events linking PR 562 and consumer issue 6, then gained its merge
reference `fc2dee2`. Each response held fewer than the requested 100 events.
Withdrawn issue 3 and reciprocal dependency links were read as context, not
completion evidence. Consumer issue 6's timeline holds no implementation report.

PR 561 is merged at `130fb09`, with all 19 checks successful on `6121838`.
PR 562 changed during review: initial head `38542eb` failed coverage
99.19% → 98.9%; `4a8b795` added service/controller/query tests, all 19 checks
passed, and it merged at `fc2dee2`. The old failure is historical, not a current
blocker. The linked report describes fresh-agent discovery; it supplies no
independently observed transcript. The existing installed companion link remains
broken, and the public mapper's malformed-required-data guarantee remains unmet.
The [reconciliation assessment](../reconciliation-20261004.md#cabinet-assignment-review--2026-10-06)
holds the artifact-based findings and concrete remaining evidence.

This is an observed builder replay, not independent operator grading or a fresh
Workshop startup. No issue response, acceptance, closure, dependency release,
commit or push was performed. The review correction is installed locally.
